  "description": "issue #792: `tell [ :a :b ]` then a single `set_xy 50 25` applies once per addressed turtle, emitting one `move`+`draw-segment` pair per turtle carrying its own `turtle_id` (1 then 2) — `set_xy` moves to an absolute point leaving heading untouched, so no `turn` fires (spec/commands.md's `set_xy` entry). Each turtle moves from its `(0,0)` heading-`0` origin to `(50,25)`. The events are stamped because the addressed set is now explicit (a `tell` has run). Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }` (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193). Closes the `set_xy` execution-coverage gap the Sprites Epic Gate recorded (issue #792): `set_xy` shares the `runPerTurtleCommand` loop and its position-command dispatch predicate with `home`, but had no Sprites-addressed execution fixture of its own.",
